From: Eric Lemesre <eric.lemesre@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 19:30:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] fix(tools-pack): lintian overrides + license + drop
 bundled cruft; state scope
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Address deb review feedback:
- Add a checked-in /usr/share/lintian/overrides/open-design documenting the
  deviations inherent to a bundled Electron package (VS Code / Slack pattern).
- fpm --license Apache-2.0 (control License was "unknown").
- Exclude bundled cruft: eslint configs (package-contains-eslint-config-file)
  and node-pty's Windows-only winpty build sources (python3 shebangs never run
  on Linux). Removes those errors and trims the package.
- resolveLinuxBuilderTargets: comment why Linux `all` == AppImage only
  (asymmetric with Windows; deb needs a separate run — mutually exclusive
  productName).
- README: state scope explicitly — .deb is build-only (lifecycle/smoke stay
  AppImage-only, no dpkg -i smoke yet; release/CI/landing not wired;
  signing/APT repo deferred), and .rpm is the planned next increment.

Verified on a fresh --to deb build: lintian-clean (0 E / 0 W with overrides),
Maintainer is a neutral project address, License: Apache-2.0, package boots.
